6401641 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\,$ $x$ is a member of the set of integer numbers.\n\nThe predicate $P(x)$ is given above. Which of following represents $¬P(x)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401641 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2fa22fb7-c16d-5dc4-beee-381645b3cb56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401641 #edb/ref 1074 "The symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. \n\nTo negate our plain English sentence, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ is a member of the set of integer numbers.\n\nIn other words, $x$ is *not* a member of the set of integer numbers. Therefore, $¬P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is **not** a member of the set of integer numbers." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401642 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401642 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401642 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401642 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401642 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186401647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401642 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401642 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401642 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186401647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401642 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6588a6a5-4237-5a1f-91da-7b37766d0fa5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401643 #edb/ref 1080 "$x$ is not a member of the set of real numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401643 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401643 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aa68b75b-8128-5a25-b790-f2663b29914e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401644 #edb/ref 1080 "$x$ is a member of the set of integer numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401644 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401