/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430207 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6bd67b3c-2b82-5f26-85f7-a27a12134ac9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430208 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430208 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430184 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430208 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430208 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430208 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430208 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430208 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430208 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186430190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430208 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "756361aa-d5cf-55f5-9c74-7d766195b840" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186430192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430210 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430210 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430210 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186430181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430210 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a9fb1666-ac67-59fa-9a0b-88ff4f949f8d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430213 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430213 #edb/ref 1069 "q-175518" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430213 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430213 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the truth set of $¬P(x)$ given the following predicate defined over the universal set $R:$\n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x-7<-9$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430213 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2f501796-fc0b-5879-8eb1-568ded583cc8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430213 #edb/ref 1074 "The truth set of $¬P(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{¬P}={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\n$$\n\nTo find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-7 & <-9 \\\\ x & <-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n${T}_{P}=(-\\infty ,-2).$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{¬P} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P} \\\\  & =\\overset{―}{(-\\infty ,-2)} \\\\  & =[-2,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430215 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430215 #edb/ref 1069 "q-176028" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430215 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430215 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\,$ $x\\ge y$\n\nThe predicate $P(x,y)$ is given above. Which of following represents $¬P(x,y)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430215 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8f075ba4-7815-572a-b12a-c4691f9f8fab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430215 #edb/ref 1074 "In plain English, our predicate $P(x,y)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is greater than or equal to $y.$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. To negate our plain English expression, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ is greater than or equal to $y.$\n\nIn other words, $x$ is *smaller than* $y.$ Therefore, $¬P(x,y)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x<y$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430216 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430216 #edb/ref 1069 "q-175313" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430216 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430216 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\,$ $x≱\\pi $\n\nThe predicate $P(x)$ is given above. Which of following represents $¬P(x)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430216 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f94afce2-6e2a-536a-8567-c4c1dfc21cb5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186430216 #edb/ref 1074 "In plain English, our predicate $P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x$ is not greater than or equal to $\\pi .$\n\nThe symbol \"$¬$\" represents negation. To negate our plain English expression, we place the words \"It is not true that\" in front of it. This gives the following:\n\n$\\,$ It is not true that $x$ is not greater than or equal to $\\pi .$\n\nIn other words, $x$ *is* *greater than or equal to* $\\pi .$ Therefore, $¬P(x)$ means the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x\\ge \\pi $" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
